# Project notes for the factory

The factory agents read the section that matches their job. Keep each short.

## Product
What this project is, who it is for, and what is out of scope. Intake uses this
to reject requests that belong elsewhere.

## Security hot spots
Routers, uploads, secrets, tokens, queries built from user input, files that must
never be committed. The security reviewer checks each against the diff.

## UI conventions
Where the theme and shared components live, and which component library to prefer.

## Users
Who uses the product, on what device, and what matters most to them
(speed, clarity, no lost work, ...).

## Always escalate
Changes a human must always see before merge (pricing logic, paid third-party
accounts, data migrations, how secrets are read, ...).
